title: Constituent Assembly Elections
subtitle: The scheduled elections have arrived...
new-page: true
view-if: (year = 1917 and month = 11 and week = 3) and ca_scheduled = 1
max-visits: 1
tags: event

= Constituent Assembly Elections

The convocation of a constituent assembly – a body to finally draft a free constitution for all Russia – has long been an aim of our Party, and a central theme in our propaganda the past few months especially. Although the Kerensky government scheduled elections, we maintain his corrupt and dysfunctional government would never have actually followed through, necessitating that we step in ourselves. The October Revolution was justified partially in the name of protecting and upholding the promise for a constituent assembly, and since then our government has technically been a "provisional" one, until the Constituent Assembly could be elected and deliberate on a more permanent system. 

Numerous delays have already occurred in the election process, which we were quick to complain about back when it was Kerensky's responsibility. Now another scheduled date has arrived, and we are under considerable pressure – both outside our party and within – to follow through on our promise to hold elections. 

With the working-class at our back, we shall prove once and for all the support and strength of our party, and use the Constituent Assembly as an opportunity to legitimize and codify the new form of soviet government going forward.

These are expected to be the largest and most progressive elections seen in world history thus far: full universal suffrage (including for women), an equal, direct, and secret ballot, without any property qualifications or restrictions based on class, religion, or nationality. 

Due to the difficulties of holding elections across the vast country, it will likely take several days to cast and count all the votes—perhaps weeks in some districts. 


- @delay_the_elections
- @cancel_the_elections
- @begin_the_elections


@delay_the_elections
title: Can we delay again? 
choose-if: moderate_strength <= 15
unavailable-subtitle: There is not enough support within the Party for this. 

@cancel_the_elections
title: Cancel the elections!
choose-if: moderate_strength <= 5
unavailable-subtitle: There is not enough support within the Party for this. 

@begin_the_elections
title: Let us begin the elections...
new-page: true
go-t0: election_strategy

@election_strategy

With the elections officially beginning, now is the time to launch any remaining electoral initiatives. 

